1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,658
Hi! This is Seoul's '성수동' [seong-su-dong],

2
00:00:02,658 --> 00:00:07,257
full of red-brick buildings and lovely cafes.

3
00:00:07,257 --> 00:00:07,871
Today,

4
00:00:07,871 --> 00:00:16,150
let's learn to describe a person's '외모' [oe-mo] (looks) and '성격' [seong-gyeok] (personality) in Korean!

5
00:00:18,950 --> 00:00:23,009
When we introduce a friend or describe someone,

6
00:00:23,009 --> 00:00:26,982
we say how they look — '생기다' [saeng-gi-da] — and their '성격' [seong-gyeok].

7
00:00:26,982 --> 00:00:30,350
Just two things: looks and personality!

8
00:00:36,010 --> 00:00:42,189
We describe people mostly with '형용사' [hyeong-yong-sa] (adjectives) — words for qualities.

9
00:00:42,189 --> 00:00:45,794
Let's meet today's expressions one by one,

10
00:00:45,794 --> 00:00:47,510
walking through 성수동.

11
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:53,706
First, height. If someone is tall: '키가 크다' [ki-ga keu-da].

12
00:00:53,706 --> 00:00:57,310
That person walking by — '키가 커요' [ki-ga keo-yo].

13
00:01:00,380 --> 00:01:04,339
The opposite: '키가 작다' [ki-ga jak-tta] (short).

14
00:01:04,339 --> 00:01:08,561
'작다' [jak-tta] is the adjective for small.

15
00:01:08,561 --> 00:01:11,200
A child is '키가 작아요' [ki-ga ja-ga-yo].

16
00:01:14,650 --> 00:01:19,071
Now hairstyle. Long hair: '머리가 길다' [meo-ri-ga gil-da].

17
00:01:19,071 --> 00:01:22,860
That cafe owner has '머리가 길어요' [meo-ri-ga gi-reo-yo].

18
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:33,075
Short hair: '머리가 짧다' [meo-ri-ga jjal-da]. '짧다' [jjal-da] is for short length.

19
00:01:33,075 --> 00:01:36,580
The barista has '머리가 짧아요' [meo-ri-ga jjal-ba-yo].

20
00:01:40,010 --> 00:01:44,262
If something is lovely to look at: '예쁘다' [ye-ppeu-da] (pretty).

21
00:01:44,262 --> 00:01:47,238
Use it for people and things alike.

22
00:01:47,238 --> 00:01:50,810
This flower — and that person — are '예뻐요' [ye-ppeo-yo].

23
00:01:54,310 --> 00:01:57,582
For a handsome face: '잘생기다' [jal-saeng-gi-da].

24
00:01:57,582 --> 00:02:02,490
Often used for men, but not only. '잘생겼어요' [jal-saeng-gyeo-sseo-yo]!

25
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:09,875
성수동 is full of stylish people, right?

26
00:02:09,875 --> 00:02:13,938
For someone chic and impressive: '멋있다' [meo-sit-tta].

27
00:02:13,938 --> 00:02:16,960
That outfit is really '멋있어요' [meo-si-sseo-yo].

28
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:23,105
Slim and trim: '날씬하다' [nal-ssin-ha-da].

29
00:02:23,105 --> 00:02:27,830
And if someone wears glasses: '안경을 쓰다' [an-gyeong-eul sseu-da].

30
00:02:33,230 --> 00:02:35,264
Now personality.

31
00:02:35,264 --> 00:02:40,604
Warm and helpful to others: '친절하다' [chin-jeol-ha-da] (kind).

32
00:02:40,604 --> 00:02:45,690
The cafe staff in 성수동 are really '친절해요' [chin-jeol-hae-yo].

33
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:50,694
Kind-hearted and helpful: '착하다' [cha-ka-da].

34
00:02:50,694 --> 00:02:57,524
Similar to '친절하다' [chin-jeol-ha-da], but '착하다' [cha-ka-da] is about the heart.

35
00:02:57,524 --> 00:03:00,370
That child is '착해요' [cha-kae-yo].

36
00:03:04,130 --> 00:03:08,524
Fun to be around and funny: '재미있다' [jae-mi-it-tta].

37
00:03:08,524 --> 00:03:14,550
The opposite is '재미없다' [jae-mi-eop-tta]. My friend is so '재미있어요' [jae-mi-i-sseo-yo].

38
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:23,540
Quiet and calm, few words: '조용하다' [jo-yong-ha-da].

39
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:25,826
The opposite of loud.

40
00:03:25,826 --> 00:03:29,200
That customer is always '조용해요' [jo-yong-hae-yo].

41
00:03:31,930 --> 00:03:36,842
Bright and full of energy: '활발하다' [hwal-bal-ha-da] (lively).

42
00:03:36,842 --> 00:03:39,355
The opposite of quiet.

43
00:03:39,355 --> 00:03:43,810
The kids running around 성수동 are '활발해요' [hwal-bal-hae-yo].

44
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:48,896
Bright and clever: '똑똑하다' [ttok-tto-ka-da] (smart).

45
00:03:48,896 --> 00:03:52,032
Understands anything quickly.

46
00:03:52,032 --> 00:03:55,060
That student is very '똑똑해요' [ttok-tto-kae-yo].

47
00:03:57,690 --> 00:04:00,360
Now let's learn '-고' [--go],

48
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:06,719
which joins two things in one sentence. It's easy.

49
00:04:06,719 --> 00:04:11,805
Take an adjective's base form, drop '다' [da],

50
00:04:11,805 --> 00:04:18,164
and add '고' [go]. '크다' [keu-da] becomes '크고' [keu-go], '작다' [jak-tta] becomes '작고' [jak-kko],

51
00:04:18,164 --> 00:04:20,453
'길다' [gil-da] becomes '길고' [gil-go].

52
00:04:20,453 --> 00:04:25,794
Only the last word gets the polite ending,

53
00:04:25,794 --> 00:04:29,990
and the first one just stays '고' [go].

54
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:43,418
Let's build one. '키가 크다' [ki-ga keu-da] and '친절하다' [chin-jeol-ha-da].

55
00:04:43,418 --> 00:04:49,139
The first becomes '크고' [keu-go], the last stays '친절해요' [chin-jeol-hae-yo].

56
00:04:49,139 --> 00:04:53,990
Together: '키가 크고 친절해요' [ki-ga keu-go chin-jeol-hae-yo] — tall and kind.

57
00:04:53,990 --> 00:04:57,970
Looks first, personality second.

58
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:07,189
One more. '머리가 길다' [meo-ri-ga gil-da] and '예쁘다' [ye-ppeu-da].

59
00:05:07,189 --> 00:05:14,139
'길다' [gil-da] becomes '길고' [gil-go], '예쁘다' [ye-ppeu-da] becomes '예뻐요' [ye-ppeo-yo].

60
00:05:14,139 --> 00:05:21,268
So: '머리가 길고 예뻐요' [meo-ri-ga gil-go ye-ppeo-yo] — long hair and pretty.

61
00:05:21,268 --> 00:05:24,120
See the pattern?

62
00:05:24,860 --> 00:05:30,244
You can join two looks, or two personalities, too.

63
00:05:30,244 --> 00:05:36,058
'재미있다' [jae-mi-it-tta] and '활발하다' [hwal-bal-ha-da] become '재미있고 활발해요' [jae-mi-it-kko hwal-bal-hae-yo] — fun and lively.

64
00:05:36,058 --> 00:05:40,580
Two or three, just keep linking with '-고' [--go].

65
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:47,112
Now describe people in '성수동' [seong-su-dong].

66
00:05:47,112 --> 00:05:51,216
One is '키가 작고 조용해요' [ki-ga jak-kko jo-yong-hae-yo] — short and quiet.

67
00:05:51,216 --> 00:05:55,428
Another is '멋있고 똑똑해요' [meo-sit-kko ttok-tto-kae-yo] — cool and smart.

68
00:05:55,428 --> 00:06:00,180
Freely link looks and personality with '-고' [--go].

69
00:06:01,230 --> 00:06:07,168
Let's introduce a friend with all we learned: '제 친구는 머리가 길고 친절해요.

70
00:06:07,168 --> 00:06:08,356
그리고 정말 재미있어요.

71
00:06:08,356 --> 00:06:12,650
' Linking sentences makes an introduction flow.

72
00:06:13,150 --> 00:06:15,912
Let's wrap up.

73
00:06:15,912 --> 00:06:24,592
Looks: '크다' [keu-da], '작다' [jak-tta], '길다' [gil-da], '짧다' [jjal-da], '예쁘다' [ye-ppeu-da], '멋있다' [meo-sit-tta].

74
00:06:24,592 --> 00:06:33,075
Personality: '친절하다' [chin-jeol-ha-da], '착하다' [cha-ka-da], '조용하다' [jo-yong-ha-da], '활발하다' [hwal-bal-ha-da],

75
00:06:33,075 --> 00:06:39,980
'똑똑하다'. And link the two with '-고' [--go].

76
00:06:44,030 --> 00:06:45,219
Now, as you walk,

77
00:06:45,219 --> 00:06:50,813
describe people in your head: '저 사람은 키가 크고 멋있어요' — that person is tall and cool.

78
00:06:50,813 --> 00:06:53,820
A little each day, and you'll improve fast.

79
00:06:54,610 --> 00:06:56,092
You did great today!

80
00:06:56,092 --> 00:07:00,018
Now you can describe someone's looks and personality,

81
00:07:00,018 --> 00:07:02,240
linked with '-고' [--go], beautifully.

82
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:06,908
Try introducing the people around you with today's expressions.

83
00:07:06,908 --> 00:07:09,130
See you next time — '안녕히 가세요' [an-nyeong-hi ga-se-yo]!

